From: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 09:14:09 +1000
Subject: soc: sunxi: Add VeriSilicon VIP9000 NPU core driver for Allwinner A733

Port and integrate the VeriSilicon VIP9000 NPU core driver (vipcore) into
drivers/soc/sunxi/npu/ to expose the /dev/galcore character device for Allwinner A733.

The A733 SoC features a VeriSilicon VIP9000 NPU providing 3 TOPS of INT8 neural
network acceleration. Mainline Linux lacked driver support for this IP. In addition,
two hardware constraints must be satisfied at boot:
1. The 512KB on-chip dedicated SRAM is disconnected from the VIP9000 by default;
   the driver configures the SYSCTRL SRAM Remap register (0x03000008 bit 1 = 0)
   to route this memory to the NPU's internal bus.
2. Hardware register access and DMA are blocked by Secure EL3 security filters
   in TF-A / BL31; the driver executes an ARM Secure Monitor Call (SMC fastcall
   0xC000FF06) during initialization to un-gate CCMU, IOMMU, and SPC permissions.

This enablement allows unprivileged userspace runtimes (including VIPLite, lenet,
and vpm_run) to run AI inference models at full hardware performance with GIC
interrupt 440 handling completion events.

Signed-off-by: Vivante Corporation <support@verisilicon.com>
Signed-off-by: Allwinner Technology Co., Ltd. <service@allwinnertech.com>
Signed-off-by: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Assisted-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>

---
